  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rehabilitation/construction of typhoon resistant houses &amp; sanitation facilities post Typhoon Haiyan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a component of Cordaid&apos;s &#x201c;Resilient Communities Projects&#x201d; which has been developed to address the recovery needs of two communities of Ngolos and Sulangan, Eastern Samar, following the devastation of Typhoon Yolanda. The objective is to deliver recovery programming which is community driven and managed. The approach utilises a resilience framework and through a participatory assessment of risk, allows for reflection of local hazards and their changes over time. This allows for adaptation of behaviour, identification of capacity gaps and the development of a community action plan. This component of the overall project will focus on 200 houses that were identified through the process and will be rebuilt through a community driven and managed approach. 
 
[Cordaid Project Number 111343]</narrative>
  </description>
